BIT-10: List each node's links once per hydraulic step and prefetch their segments

Every quality step, topological_transport() walked each node's adjacency
list twice and added up its outflow rate again, although flows, demands
and flow directions change only when a hydraulic solution is read.

1. buildTransportPlan() lists, once per hydraulic step and for each node
   in topological order, the links with flow into it, the links with flow
   out of it (each in adjacency-list order) and its outflow rate, summed
   in the same order as before. The node loop streams through these
   arrays. A redundant clear of SourceIn is removed.
2. Before each node, the loop prefetches the leading segment of each
   inflow link and the last segment of each outflow link of the node two
   places ahead in topological order (__builtin_prefetch; a no-op on
   compilers without it).

Requires: none
Results: identical (every concentration, the output file and the report are unchanged)

Apply from the root of an EPANET-MSX checkout at 85a303d, after FIX-01, FIX-02 and BIT-01 to BIT-09:
    git apply --whitespace=nowarn BIT-10.patch
or use tools/build-msx.sh, which applies the series in order.

